	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42205</id><title>Cuts Stall Clinical Trials, Scientists Warn US Risks Losing Its Research Edge</title><updated>2026-01-27T13:38:55-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42205" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/scientists.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/scientists.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
URBANA, Illinois, US, January 27 (IPS)  - Scientists across the U.S., including me, are stressed after a &lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/theconversation.com/this-year-nearly-broke-me-as-a-scientist-us-researchers-reflect-on-how-2025s-science-cuts-have-changed-their-lives-271282__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sCteqDo0$&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/theconversation.com/this-year-nearly-broke-me-as-a-scientist-us-researchers-reflect-on-how-2025s-science-cuts-have-changed-their-lives-271282__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sCteqDo0$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1769596750298000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pkEaF8OpM0rcUXo3l4ara&quot;&gt;year marked by several changes&lt;/a&gt; and challenges, including cuts to &lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.sciencenews.org/article/nih-nsf-cuts-2025-data__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sKqH7LEA$&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.sciencenews.org/article/nih-nsf-cuts-2025-data__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sKqH7LEA$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1769596750298000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UObCYMFrgu_Z-M7qf1_kk&quot;&gt;science funding&lt;/a&gt; that have stalled clinical trials and studies that could improve and save lives. Without funding, scientists worry about how they will support ongoing research and train America’s future workforce, including the &lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.alicoalition.org/blog/science-cuts-threaten-the-next-generation-of-innovators/__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sHNdA0mw$&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.alicoalition.org/blog/science-cuts-threaten-the-next-generation-of-innovators/__;!!DZ3fjg!7MF31v4IsyyiUyf24o7vKsoHwX1uviUgfVqB0vdPn_zMsvT5fBB_b3n1-KUCqkxzfyVhkoYUIP0zDL_sHNdA0mw$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1769596750298000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qo9umyMb9W3dTCqy90NWA&quot;&gt;next generation of innovators&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42205&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Cuts Stall Clinical Trials, Scientists Warn US Risks Losing Its Research Edge”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/scientists-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42203</id><title>Binalakshmi Nepram: Engineering Peace, Creating History</title><updated>2026-01-27T13:29:56-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42203" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Binalakshmi-Nepram-Photo-by-Nobel-Women-Initiative.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Binalakshmi-Nepram-Photo-by-Nobel-Women-Initiative.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
NEW DELHI, January 27 (IPS)  - It was Christmas eve: some two decades ago. Binalakshmi Nepram was a witness to the killing of a 27-year-old.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42203&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Binalakshmi Nepram: Engineering Peace, Creating History”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Binalakshmi-Nepram-Photo-by-Nobel-Women-Initiative-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42204</id><title>A Not So Happy United States</title><updated>2026-01-27T12:54:44-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42204" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/happinessrankingfeatured.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/happinessrankingfeatured.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
PORTLAND, USA, January 27 (IPS)  - The United States is not so happy. Its population has received a lower &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wmtw.com/article/united-states-lowest-ranking-world-happiness-report/65381042#:~:text=%2C%22%20he%20says.-,Another%20reason%20for%20this%20ranking%20is%20the%20increasing%20amount%20of,:%20eat%2C%20sleep%2C%20exercise.&quot;&gt;happiness ranking&lt;/a&gt; compared to previous years. The factors contributing to this decline have significant implications for the United States, both domestically and internationally. As Dostoevsky noted, “The greatest happiness is to know the source of unhappiness”.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42204&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “A Not So Happy United States”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/happinessrankingfeatured-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42202</id><title>As Korea Ages, Fiscal Reforms Can Help Safeguard Government Finances</title><updated>2026-01-27T07:38:12-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42202" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/imf-country_45.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/imf-country_45.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
WASHINGTON DC, January 27 (IPS)  - Korea’s population is aging faster than almost any other country. That’s because people live longer than in most other countries, while the birth rate is one of the lowest in the world.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42202&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “As Korea Ages, Fiscal Reforms Can Help Safeguard Government Finances”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/imf-country_45-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42210</id><title>Yemen: Security Council votes on final extension of Hudaydah Mission</title><updated>2026-01-27T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42210" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/12-02-2025_UNMHA_flag.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/12-02-2025_UNMHA_flag.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Security Council adopted a resolution on Tuesday that renews the mandate of the UN Mission in the Yemeni port city of Hudaydah for a final two-month period through 31 March of this year. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42210&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Yemen: Security Council votes on final extension of Hudaydah Mission”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/12-02-2025_UNMHA_flag.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42209</id><title>From lunch tray to lifelong health: WHO sets global standards for school meals</title><updated>2026-01-27T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42209" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/22-01-2026-UNICEF-Rwanda.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/22-01-2026-UNICEF-Rwanda.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For the first time ever, the World Health Organization (WHO) is providing recommendations for healthy and nutritious food in schools around the world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42209&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “From lunch tray to lifelong health: WHO sets global standards for school meals”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/22-01-2026-UNICEF-Rwanda.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42208</id><title>UN says Gaza crisis remains dire, children hardest hit</title><updated>2026-01-27T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42208" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/07-11-2025-WFP-Gaza-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/07-11-2025-WFP-Gaza-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Despite a modest increase in humanitarian assistance, the situation in Gaza remains “dire”, with children among the hardest hit by shortages of shelter, basic services and education, the United Nations said on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42208&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN says Gaza crisis remains dire, children hardest hit”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/07-11-2025-WFP-Gaza-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42207</id><title>Remembering the Holocaust: ‘You are here because you choose hope over hate’</title><updated>2026-01-27T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42207" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/27-01-2026-UN-Photo-GA-Holocaust.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/27-01-2026-UN-Photo-GA-Holocaust.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Holocaust is a warning, that hatred “can consume everything” – a message that feels more urgent than ever, the UN chief said on Tuesday, as antisemitism rages worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42207&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Remembering the Holocaust: ‘You are here because you choose hope over hate’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/27-01-2026-UN-Photo-GA-Holocaust.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42206</id><title>Independent experts alarmed by child rights violations in US immigration procedures</title><updated>2026-01-27T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42206" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-01-2024_Unsplash_US-Capitol.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-01-2024_Unsplash_US-Capitol.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN-appointed independent human rights experts have raised alarm over violations of children’s rights during US immigration procedures, nearly a year after federal funding for legal representation for unaccompanied minors was terminated. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/27/42206&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Independent experts alarmed by child rights violations in US immigration procedures”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-01-2024_Unsplash_US-Capitol.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/26/42193</id><title>Uganda: Democracy in Name Only</title><updated>2026-01-26T11:18:37-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/26/42193" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Abubaker-Lubowa_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Abubaker-Lubowa_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
MONTEVIDEO, Uruguay, January 26 (IPS)  - When Ugandans went to the polls on 15 January, the outcome was never in doubt. As voting began, mobile internet services ground to a halt, ensuring minimal scrutiny as President Yoweri Museveni secured his seventh consecutive term. Far from offering democratic choice, the vote reinforced one of Africa’s longest-running presidencies, providing a veneer of democratic legitimacy while stifling competition.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/01/26/42193&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Uganda: Democracy in Name Only”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/01/Abubaker-Lubowa_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry></feed><!-- 0.0016s -->